:: R4_Harper_Interaction [r4 story]
<<location "Floor 39, Daniel's Desk">>
<<portrait "files/images/mood/r4-npc-harper-desk.webp" "Harper Quinn">>
<<objective "Handle Harper's questions.">>

Harper catches me at my desk an hour later. She's carrying two coffees. Sets one on my desk without asking. Black, no sugar. She knows.

<<say "Harper Quinn">>You blanked during the standup this morning.<</say>>

<<sayself>>I was distracted.<</sayself>>

<<say "Harper Quinn">>You're never distracted.<</say>>

She sits on the edge of my desk. She does this. It's a Harper thing. Perching on surfaces, occupying space with a casual ownership that belies her junior title.

<<say "Harper Quinn">>And then the stutter during Whitmore. Are you sleeping okay?<</say>>

<<sayself>>Fine.<</sayself>>

<<say "Harper Quinn">>You keep shifting in your chair. Like you're uncomfortable.<</say>>

The observation is precise. Clinical. She's been watching me all day. Filing.

<<sayself>>New suit. The tailor cut the inseam too tight.<</sayself>>

She looks at my suit. Looks at me. Her expression doesn't change but something behind her eyes flickers. She doesn't believe me. Harper rarely believes explanations that arrive too quickly.

<<say "Harper Quinn">>Okay.<</say>>

She picks up her coffee. Takes a sip. Doesn't leave.

<<say "Harper Quinn">>Victoria Cross sat in on your presentation. She never sits in on Floor 39 meetings.<</say>>

<<sayself>>She's the new vertical lead. She's reviewing everything.<</sayself>>

<<say "Harper Quinn">>She was watching you. Not the presentation. You.<</say>>

I take a drink of the coffee she brought me. It's too hot. I drink it anyway.

<<sayself>>She watches everyone. That's her thing.<</sayself>>

Harper slides off my desk. Straightens her blazer.

<<say "Harper Quinn">>Let me know if you need anything, Daniel. I mean that.<</say>>

She walks away. I watch her go. She doesn't look back, but I know she's still watching. Harper Quinn never stops watching. It's her greatest skill and, depending on how the next few months unfold, it might be my greatest liability.

